# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# IQRA web — example env
# Every value here is PUBLIC: it ends up baked into the JS bundle and visible
# in the browser's view-source. NEVER put secrets here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Google Sign-In (Phase 2) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same Web Client ID as the backend's GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID. Cloud Console →
# Authorized JavaScript origins must list every URL the SPA is served from
# (http://localhost:3000 in dev, https://iqra.app in prod).
VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# ─── Facebook / Instagram login (Phase 3) ─────────────────────────────────
# App ID only (App Secret stays server-side). Once you flip the Meta app to
# Live, add https://iqra.app to Valid OAuth Redirect URIs.
# VITE_FACEBOOK_APP_ID=

# ─── Cloudflare Turnstile (Phase 6) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Site key (public). The secret stays in the backend's .env.
# Test key below — replace with the real one in prod and add `localhost` /
# the prod domain in Cloudflare's Hostname Management.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA

# ─── API base URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev: leave empty so Vite proxies /api/* to Laravel (see vite.config.ts).
# Prod: point at the deployed Laravel API. Must be HTTPS for service workers.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.iqra.app
